              {
                "text": "**Analyzing the Color Patterns**\n\nI'm now focusing on the dot color in the different training examples. It seems the background color varies across the training sets, starting with the dots, as they change with each set. In train 3, the dots have color 2. I'm starting to think the output consists of adding green lines between certain dots. I need to understand this pattern in train 1 and 2, too.\n\n\n**Investigating Row and Column**\n\nI've been examining the relationships between dots with the color 8. It seems if two dots share a row or column, a horizontal or vertical line of 3s appears between them. For instance, in training set 1, dots at (1,1) and (1,6) (same row) are connected by 3s. Similarly, (1,1) and (4,1) (same column) have a vertical line. However, (5,7) doesn't connect because it shares neither a row or column with another. I'm verifying this now in train 2.\n\n\n",
